From 36fecc8482efdf0ecd416b5336042be4bd0a7f4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 22:06:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] plugin_api: pause a pixel plugin when its scene is left,
 resume it on return

A pixel plugin was stopped whenever its scene was left, so going Home or
through Recents and back cold-started the app. Browser instead keeps its
runtime between scenes. Do the same for pixel plugins: leaving the scene
sends LIFECYCLE/PAUSE and withholds FRAME_DONE, so the plugin stops
drawing; opening it again (from Recents or the plugin list) sends a new
SURFACE, which gives every slot back in the current orientation, and
LIFECYCLE/RESUME. A plugin stops when it sends CLOSE, when Recents is
cleared or drops it, when an update replaces it, or on failure.

Add Lifecycle kInactive (4) for a plugin still on screen while the status
shade, a sheet or the file picker takes the input. It is appended, so
released plugins see no renumbering, and a plugin that ignores it still
behaves correctly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J6XhHxrkhAcXmkzHMeCnVz
